    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d475">

                <pb facs="1782" n="1677" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v03mSupp/pg1677"/>

                <head>475. Letter From Herter to
                        Taylor<anchor n="1" xml:id="d475-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-07-01">July 1, 1959</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear General Taylor:</salute>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d475-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d475-1"/>
                <p>This is to confirm our telephone conversation of today regarding the review of
                    U.S. disarmament policy. In accordance with our conversation, I am sending
                    herewith a copy of the terms of reference which the President has approved.</p>
                <p>As I told you, this study is of the utmost importance to us, as we will most
                    certainly be involved in one way or another in arms control and limitations
                    negotiations with the Russians in the not too distant future. Such negotiations
                    would, of course, be in addition to the current negotiations in Geneva on the
                    suspension of nuclear testing.</p>
                <p>I cannot express too strongly the hope that you will find it possible to
                    undertake the undertaken the general direction of this important review of our
                    disarmament policy and devote such time to it as your commitments will
                    permit.</p>
                <p>Most sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Christian A.
                            Herter</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d475-a1.xml" xpointer="d475-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
